{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Colour and name your tracks from what they are: your own ordered rules (import/export SWS Auto Color), instrument families with colours, palettes, gradients and nudges, name-from-items, numbering, and a LIVE mode that re-colours as tracks are added or renamed. Markers and regions too. Requires the "Shared Libraries" package from this same repository (right-click the repository in ReaPack > Install All).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Live patch switching for REAPER. Reads a setlist built by StageRig Build, shows a stage view with NOW and NEXT, and switches patches without cutting off what is still ringing. Bind "StageRig Next" / "StageRig Panic" to a footswitch for hands-free use. Requires the "Shared Libraries" package from this same repository (right-click the repository in ReaPack > Install All).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Print stems four ways (raw / to the bus / through master / fully wet) and put the session back exactly as it was. Optionally builds a plugin-free mirror tab with the printed files on it, ready to hand to anyone on any DAW. Requires the "Shared Libraries" package from this same repository (right-click the repository in ReaPack > Install All).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pro-Tools style "Import Session Data" between open project tabs. Copies FX chains, volume, pan, sends, colour and input FX from the tracks of one project onto the same-named tracks of one or more other tabs, or builds the tracks that are missing. Preview first; one undo point per target project. Automation is never copied. Requires the "Shared Libraries" package from this same repository and the SWS extension. ReaPack has no automatic dependencies, so install the libraries too - or right-click the repository in ReaPack > Install All.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Duplicate the selected track EMPTY and armed, ready to record the next layer; your original arm state comes back exactly. Needs SWS.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Puts the selected tracks into one track group for EDITING ONLY: media and razor edits on one track happen on all of them (split, trim, move, delete), while faders, mutes, solos and arms stay independent. Press it again on the same tracks to take them OUT of their edit group. The clutch: "Track: Toggle all track grouping enabled" (Jason: Cmd+Shift+G) bypasses every group while you do fine edits; press again to re-engage.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Float the first FX of the selected tracks, or close it if it is already open. Needs SWS.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Open every FX window on the selected (or last touched) track, or close them all if any are open.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Replace whatever is on the selected tracks with the clipboard: delete their items, paste, strip envelopes, save silently. Needs SWS.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Build, dissolve, move and isolate track folders without dragging. Indent / outdent ticked tracks, take a track out of its folder, move a whole folder up or down, auto-group tracks by name, and repair a session whose folder nesting has gone wrong. Requires the "Shared Libraries" package from this same repository (right-click the repository in ReaPack > Install All).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Select two (or more) tracks and press: a NEW folder track appears above them, the selected tracks go inside it, nothing else in the session changes shape. The folder is named from what the children have in common ("Kick In"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab "Kick Out" -> KICK; "Electric L/R/C" -> ELECTRIC), coloured like its\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 children, and made a little taller so it reads as a folder. Non-adjacent selections are first gathered together under the first one. Needs the Shared Libraries package (nt_hierarchy).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Export many MIDI items or regions as separate .mid files in one go, named from a pattern ($num, $name, $track, $region, $project, $bpm). Every file carries the tempo and time signature at its own start, at the item's own tick resolution, so it opens at the right speed anywhere. Requires the "Shared Libraries" package from this same repository (right-click the repository in ReaPack > Install All).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Export the project MIDI for the time selection (or the whole project if there is none) with one key.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Drop a marker on the nearest bar line to the cursor (or the play position while playing). Never in between beats, never a duplicate.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Runs quietly in the background (start it from __startup.lua or the Actions list). Every time a NEW, never-saved project appears - REAPER launch, File > New project, a new project tab - it switches snapping ON, relative grid snap ON, and transport repeat (loop) OFF. Projects you open from disk are left exactly as they were saved.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Opens Palette & Look, Folders & Flow, Track Settings Transfer, Stem Print & Handoff and MIDI Batch Export in REAPER's docker, as tabs, in one go. Run it once from the Actions list, or put it in your startup so the tools are there "at the word go". Apps that are already open are left alone. StageRig is deliberately not included - it is a stage tool, not a studio one.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Arm ONLY the selected tracks (everything else disarmed); press again to disarm all. Never touches pan, unlike the custom action it replaced.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Jump to the next region and make it the time selection. While playing, playback follows the jump (with smooth seek, on the bar).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Jump to the previous region and make it the time selection. While playing, playback follows the jump (with smooth seek, on the bar).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The shared code the rest of the Nathaniel Tools is built on: pointer safety and stable track identity (nt_safe), folder-nesting arithmetic (nt_hierarchy), and ReaImGui version compatibility (nt_imgui).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Solo-in-place the selected tracks (or the tracks of the selected items); press again on the same set to clear every solo. Never moves the cursor unless you turn AUDITION on.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires the "Shared Libraries" package from this same repository. ReaPack has no automatic dependencies, so install that one too - or just right-click the repository in ReaPack and choose Install All. Builds a live concert project from a rig spec generated out of a MainStage .concert file. Creates one folder per patch, one track per channel strip, inserts the substitute instrument where one is known, and puts the note tracker in front of every instrument so patch switching can be clean.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Tells the running StageRig window to switch to the NEXT patch. Bind this to a footswitch or MIDI pedal (Actions > find "StageRig Next" > Add shortcut > press the pedal) and you never touch the mouse on stage. Does nothing if StageRig is not open.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Tells the running StageRig window to PANIC: mute and flush every patch except the one you are playing. Bind it to a second pedal. Does nothing if StageRig is not open.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Adds a stretch marker exactly under the mouse pointer, in the item you are pointing at, without moving the edit cursor. Meant to be assigned as a mouse modifier: Preferences > Mouse modifiers > "Media item bottom half" > left click > Action list > this script. (Nathaniel Tools sets Control+click.) Needs SWS (for the mouse-position lookup).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Insert or edit a tempo / time-signature marker exactly on a bar line, with a small dialog.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Finds Chorale wherever it is in the project and flips it on/off. Bind this to a footswitch and you have hands-free harmony.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Trim the LEFT edge of the selected items to the edit cursor - and if that would push the item over its neighbour on the same track, trim the neighbour's right edge to the cursor too. Items butt, they never overlap, so no surprise crossfades. Replaces "Item edit: Trim left edge of item to edit cursor" (Jason's Z key).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Trim the RIGHT edge of the selected items to the edit cursor - and if that would push the item over its neighbour on the same track, move the neighbour's left edge to the cursor too (its audio stays in place). Items butt, they never overlap. Replaces "Item edit: Trim right edge of item to edit cursor" (Jason's X key).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Wherever two items on the same track overlap, the EARLIER item is cut at the start of the later one, so items butt instead of sitting on top of each other with a tangled crossfade. Works on the selected items; with no item selected, on every item of the selected tracks. Fades are left as they are.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Clear every solo, arm, selection and the time selection in one press. The reset key.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Held-note tracking, an input gate and a note-off/CC64 flush, for clean live patch switching. Used by StageRig, but useful on its own anywhere a MIDI stream needs to be stopped without leaving notes hanging.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Sits at the top of a patch track FX chain and decides whether new notes reach the instrument below. Never blocks note-offs; flushes held notes + CC64 on close. Superseded by Note Tracker & Input Gate for StageRig, kept for simple rigs.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs40 Nathaniel Tools\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Dockable ReaImGui apps and a keyboard speed layer for REAPER, built by a working producer for his own sessions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Jason Zac} \u183? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nathanielschool.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul Nathaniel School of Music}}} \u183? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://daw.nathanielschool.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul daw.nathanielschool.com}}}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 \i These exist because his own sessions were slow, not because anyone surveyed a market.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 \i Every app in here replaces a REAPER custom action that was quietly doing the wrong thing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Status:} 68 in-REAPER checks + 57 pure-Lua checks passing, 0 failing, against REAPER 7.77 / ReaImGui 0.10 on macOS arm64. Installed and verified end-to-end through ReaPack on the studio Mac, 19 Aug 2026.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Plain-English user guide:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "docs/USER_GUIDE.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul docs/USER_GUIDE.md}}} (also on the site at {\f1 /guide}).\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 What's in it\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 Apps (dockable, ReaImGui, one accent colour each)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 App  \u8212?  Colour  \u8212?  What it does\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b Palette & Look}  \u8212?  teal  \u8212?  Colour and name tracks from what they {\i are} \u8212? families, your own rules, palettes, live watcher.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b Folders & Flow}  \u8212?  green  \u8212?  Build, fix, dissolve, move and isolate track folders. Repairs a session whose folder maths has gone wrong.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b Track Settings Transfer}  \u8212?  green  \u8212?  Pro-Tools style "Import Session Data" across project tabs. Guesses stay unticked; transfer asks first.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b Stem Print & Handoff}  \u8212?  amber  \u8212?  Print stems (raw / inserts / fully wet / front-end), build a plugin-free handoff tab with the files on it, restore the session exactly.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b MIDI Batch Export}  \u8212?  amber  \u8212?  Export many MIDI items/regions as separate {\f1 .mid} files with pattern-based sequential names, tempo and time signature included.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b StageRig}  \u8212?  violet  \u8212?  Live patch switching that lets the outgoing patch ring out. Footswitch scripts {\f1 StageRig Next} / {\f1 StageRig Panic}. Early.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 All six windows share one look and one behaviour ({\f1 scripts/lib/nt_ui.lua}): header, sections, one primary button, a status line that always says what happened (with a log), confirmation before anything destructive, drag-paint tick columns, plain-English tooltips.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 The speed layer (12 scripts, keyboard-bound)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Solo Focus \u183? Record Arm Toggle \u183? FX Float Toggle \u183? FX Open/Close All \u183? Region Next/Prev \u183? Marker at Bar \u183? Tempo at Bar \u183? MIDI Render \u183? Flush Paste \u183? Duplicate Track \u183? Unsolo & Unselect\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each one replaced a custom action that had a real, diagnosed bug \u8212? a pan-destroying step, a global preference being toggled on every press, a marker snapping to the arrange grid instead of the bar line. The root causes are documented in {\f1 docs/TECH_BRIEF.md}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 The shared spine\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab {\b `scripts/lib/nt_safe.lua`} \u8212? pointer safety and stable identity. The reason these apps\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 cannot crash REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab {\b `scripts/lib/nt_hierarchy.lua`} \u8212? folder maths. Converts REAPER's {\f1 I_FOLDERDEPTH} integers\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 to nesting levels, edits there, and regenerates. Well-formed output by construction.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab {\b `scripts/lib/nt_ui.lua`} \u8212? the design system: tokens, fonts (ReaImGui 0.9 and 0.10),\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 window/header/button/segmented/table/status/confirm/empty. Every window uses it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab {\b `scripts/lib/nt_imgui.lua`} \u8212? bridges the enum constants ReaImGui renamed between releases.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Two things that make this different from a folder of scripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 1. It cannot crash REAPER\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER frees a {\f1 MediaTrack*} the instant the track is deleted. Handing a freed pointer to any REAPER API faults inside REAPER's own C++, and {\b Lua `pcall` cannot catch it} \u8212? the host process dies, taking unsaved projects with it. Wrapping your draw loop in {\f1 pcall} is false comfort.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Every app here stores {\b track GUIDs}, resolves them to pointers immediately before use, validates with {\f1 ValidatePtr2}, and never holds a pointer across a defer frame. The test suite deletes a track behind an app's back and asserts that every accessor returns a clean default instead of faulting.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 2. Folder edits are well-formed by construction\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Folder scripts go wrong because they edit {\f1 I_FOLDERDEPTH} in place: a local edit that looks right leaves the arithmetic unbalanced further down, and REAPER silently swallows the rest of the session into a folder.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 nt_hierarchy} never edits depths. It converts to levels, edits there, and regenerates every depth. The output always balances \u8212? it is not possible for the app to leave a folder hanging open.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires {\b [ReaImGui](https://github.com/cfillion/reaimgui)} and {\b [SWS](https://sws-extension.org)}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 With ReaPack (recommended)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This repository {\b is} a ReaPack repository. In REAPER:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tab {\b Extensions \u8594? ReaPack \u8594? Import repositories\u8230?}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tab Paste this URL and click OK:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 https://github.com/jasonzacmusic/nathaniel-tools/raw/main/index.xml}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tab {\b Extensions \u8594? ReaPack \u8594? Browse packages\u8230?}, filter on {\f1 Nathaniel Tools}, and install what you want.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Every package is signed with a SHA-256 checksum and every download is pinned to a git commit, so an installed version can never change underneath you. Updates arrive through {\b Extensions \u8594? ReaPack \u8594? Synchronize packages}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 By hand\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tab Copy {\f1 scripts/} and {\f1 apps/} somewhere REAPER can see them.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tab {\i Actions \u8594? Show action list \u8594? New action\u8230? \u8594? Load ReaScript}, and pick each app.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tab Or run {\f1 tests/harness.lua} once \u8212? it registers everything for you and verifies the install.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Publishing (maintainer notes)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 index.xml} at the repository root is the ReaPack index. It is rebuilt automatically by {\f1 .github/workflows/reapack.yml} on every push to {\f1 main}, and can be rebuilt by hand:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 python3 tools/build_index.py --check   # validate headers, write nothing}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 python3 tools/build_index.py           # rebuild index.xml}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 tools/build_index.py} is a dependency-free implementation of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://codeberg.org/cfillion/reapack/wiki/Index-Format"}}{\fldrslt{\ul ReaPack Index Format}}} \u8212? Python 3 and {\f1 git}, nothing else, and byte-identical output on any machine. CI also runs cfillion's own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul `reapack-index`}}} in {\f1 --check} mode as a second opinion on the headers.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Two rules for anything new that lands in {\f1 scripts/} or {\f1 apps/}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab Every {\f1 .lua} / {\f1 .jsfx} file needs a metadata header with at least {\f1 @version}, or it\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 fails the build. See the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index/wiki/Packaging-Documentation"}}{\fldrslt{\ul Packaging Documentation}}}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab Shared libraries carry {\f1 @noindex} and are listed in the {\f1 @provides} of the script that\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 needs them, so they install alongside it instead of appearing as their own package.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Files must live in a subdirectory \u8212? ReaPack never indexes files at the repository root, and the directory name becomes the category shown in ReaPack.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Testing\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 lua tests/hierarchy_test.lua      # 57 checks, no REAPER needed}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Inside REAPER, run {\f1 tests/harness.lua} from the action list \u8212? 68 checks including live crash-safety. It builds its scratch project {\b in its own tab} and closes it afterwards, so it never touches the project you had open. Results land in {\f1 _nt_results.txt}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 \i Edit {\f1 BASE} at the top of {\f1 harness.lua} to point at your install path.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Two REAPER API traps documented here\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Both cost real debugging time. Neither is in the official docs.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tab {\b `GetProjectStateChangeCount` does not detect track changes.} Measured in 7.77: it\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 stayed on {\f1 8} across insert, rename {\i and} delete. Any change-watchdog built on it never fires. Use a track-list signature instead.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tab {\b `ValidatePtr2` rejects `0`} \u8212? even though {\f1 0} is ReaScript's shorthand for "the\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 current project". Guards must special-case it or they return false for everything.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 More in {\f1 docs/TECH_BRIEF.md}.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
